{% comment %}
  Optimal Product Page Recommendations - Smart Single Widget
  Backend intelligently chooses the best recommendation type based on data availability
{% endcomment %}

{% assign dummy_data = 'Messenger Bag,V-Neck Tee,Deluxe Gift Box,Trail Boots,Jogger Pants,Bucket Hat|44.99,22.99,54.99,99.99,44.99,24.99|2c3e50,27ae60,e67e22,8e44ad,1abc9c,f39c12|unused|1,1,1,1,1,1'
  | split: '|'
%}

{% comment %}
  Product page only.

  Recommendations are keyed on the product being viewed, so this block needs a
  product in scope. Placed on any other template there is nothing to recommend
  against, and the backend has no surface registered for those contexts — so it
  renders nothing rather than firing a request that would be rejected.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  Storefront recommendations switched off in the app.

  Written by the admin settings page into an app-data metafield precisely so
  this decision can be made here, before any HTML exists. Without it the block
  ships its loading skeleton, JS starts, the API answers "surface_disabled", and
  the shopper watches a widget paint and then vanish — which reads as broken
  rather than switched off.

  `.value` is load-bearing. `app.metafields.config.phoenix_enabled` is a
  metafield *object*, and an object is truthy in Liquid even when the boolean it
  wraps is false — so testing the bare path would render the block no matter
  what the merchant chose. Only `.value` is the boolean.

  `default: true, allow_false: true` is also deliberate: plain `default` treats
  false as blank, so without allow_false the flag could never be off. The `true`
  default covers a shop that has never saved settings and so has no metafield —
  the previous, optimistic behaviour.

  ponytail: Liquid's copy of an app metafield can lag a change by up to an hour
  and Shopify does not reliably invalidate it. In that window this falls back to
  exactly the old behaviour — block renders, API declines, widget hides — so a
  stale read is late, never wrong.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign bb_phoenix_enabled = app.metafields.config.phoenix_enabled.value
  | default: true, allow_false: true
%}

{% comment %}
  Nested rather than one `and`/`or` chain: Liquid has no operator precedence and
  evaluates right to left, so a flat condition here would be a trap for whoever
  edits it next.

  The theme customiser is exempt from the flag — a merchant editing the block
  must be able to see it even while the surface is off.
{% endcomment %}
{% if product and product.id %}
  {% if bb_phoenix_enabled or request.design_mode %}
    {% render 'recommendation-base', context: 'product_page', product_id: product.id, dummy_data: dummy_data %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product",
  "target": "section",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Section Heading" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "You might also like"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_size",
      "label": "Heading Size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "h1", "label": "H1" },
        { "value": "h2", "label": "H2" },
        { "value": "h3", "label": "H3" },
        { "value": "h4", "label": "H4" }
      ],
      "default": "h3"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_alignment",
      "label": "Heading Alignment",
      "options": [
        { "value": "left", "label": "Left" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "Center" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "Right" }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "heading_color", "label": "Heading Color" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_heading", "label": "Show Heading", "default": true },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Recommendations" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "limit",
      "label": "Number of Products",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 8,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 6
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Card Styles" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Leave colours empty to inherit your theme's own colours and fonts. Set one only where you want to override." },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "card_border_radius",
      "label": "Card Border Radius",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 8
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "card_bg", "label": "Card Background" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "title_color", "label": "Title Color" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "price_color", "label": "Price Color" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "button_bg", "label": "Button Background" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "button_text", "label": "Button Text Color" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "button_border_radius",
      "label": "Button Border Radius",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 6
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Controls" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_arrows", "label": "Show Arrows", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_pagination", "label": "Show Pagination", "default": true },
    { "type": "color", "id": "pagination_color", "label": "Pagination Color" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_autoplay", "label": "Enable autoplay (desktop only)", "default": true },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Autoplay is off on phones by design — it competes with scrolling, and there is no hover to pause it. Shoppers swipe instead." },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "autoplay_delay",
      "label": "Autoplay Delay (seconds)",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 10,
      "step": 0.5,
      "default": 2.5,
      "unit": "s"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
